      "id": 14838,
      "name": "Voob Gooblin",
      "username": "Voob_Gooblin",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/voob_gooblin/{size}/2504_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-03-17T20:24:12.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I am curious: who here has beaten Bugbear, and how did you do it?</p><p>I've played I think 4 games against him now and won just once, and that was using the Unhallowed Halls / Twist the Ether exploit that felt like cheating. Of the 3 definitely legitimate games, I only managed to incapacitate him once and I was still not at all close to winning the game, having left the other villains free to wreak havoc.</p><p>The HP gain he has on every attack (along with his high starting HP) and the damage increase via incapacitated cards, I feel, should make him a level 4 on the difficulty scale. Plus, Quetzalcoatl is brutal—</p><p>or have I just been unlucky/missing the right strategy?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:47:02.203Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 5,
